---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Care Guide — Ramia Studio" lang="en">
  <main class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-16 md:py-24 min-h-[70vh]">
    <article class="prose prose-neutral prose-sm sm:prose-base mx-auto font-body text-neutral-700 font-light leading-relaxed space-y-6 prose-headings:font-display prose-headings:font-normal prose-headings:tracking-wide">
      
      <h1 class="font-display text-4xl text-neutral-900 mb-8 font-normal tracking-wide">Care Guide</h1>
      <p>Acrylic is a durable and ultra-light material, but it requires care to maintain its structural shine and mirror effect.</p>
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-neutral-900 mt-10 mb-4 font-normal tracking-wide">How to Clean</h2>
      <p>Always use a <strong>soft, dry microfiber cloth</strong>. For stubborn marks, slightly dampen the cloth with water.</p>
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-neutral-900 mt-10 mb-4 font-normal tracking-wide">What NEVER to do</h2>
      <p><strong>Avoid direct alcohol and perfumes:</strong> Chemical solvents, including cologne, hairspray, or alcohol, can cause irreparable micro-cracks in the acrylic material.</p>
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-neutral-900 mt-10 mb-4 font-normal tracking-wide">Storage</h2>
      <p>Store your Ramia in their original box or pouch, separated from other metal jewelry to prevent friction scratches.</p>
  
    </article>
  </main>
</Layout>